ble in the box  of course you have to buy that  separately or use one that you already  have  now there are a couple of really great  benefits with this one compared to other  options  and that is that you'll actually get a  notification on your phone as far as the  charge capacity  so that is very convenient and this  battery pack  will allow reverse wireless charging  with your iphone  12s and that is a feature that people  waiting for for a while  but unfortunately it is only to charge  the battery pack  itself now another cool feature that you  get which you get with most of these  is that you can use it as a wireless  charging base station so you can plug it  in at your desk  set your phone on top and when you're  ready to go you just pick it up  you don't need a dedicated wireless  charger so it can pass through  that is really cool and it'll wait till  your phone's charged until it charges  the internal battery  but with that you can actually plug in  your phone  and then it'll charge your phone and  once it's done it will reverse  wirelessly charge the battery pack as  well  now personally that is not that exciting  to me because if i'm on a fast charge  i'll plug in my phone  and the only time i'm going to leave it  plugged in that long to charge my phone  and then the battery pack is at night  in that case i might as well just plug  the pack in itself what i really want  reverse wireless charging for  is for air pods and an apple watch would  be amazing  to be able to charge from your iphone  other than that info  there is very little details about the  charging speed how much charge you will  actually get  or what the capacity is which apple did  actually state with their previous  smart battery case it will tell you how  much of the charge your phone will get  from it  and that is a little bit worrisome but  if we go ahead and look into  apple's dedicated page that has extra  info we get a few really important  points  and we can also find a page which helps  you find the serial number  but there zoomed in we actually see the  capacity which is a thousand four  hundred and sixty milliamp  hours that is super low but doesn't tell  the whole story  so this one right here that i have is  4200 this one's 5 000 so 14  60 is low but the voltage is actually  double what you typically have inside  your phone or inside  of these battery packs that you can buy  that means if we do the math the actual  milliamp  hours is about 29.20 so that is much  better  and that is slightly higher than an  iphone 12 or 12 pro  lower than the pro max but it is still  not  as good as these which have larger  batteries  and of course that 10.8 watt hour  battery rating  is just the battery itself that doesn't  account for inefficiencies  when you're pulling energy from a  battery or inefficiencies  when you're on top of that wirelessly  charging  most battery banks that use a cable to  charge your phone they have  80 to 90 efficiency 90 is  very very good the best of the best and  then on top of that you have loss from  wireless charging  so most of these mag saves when i tested  it  their actual efficiency was about 45  to 48 of the rated one so this one  from a 5 000 milliamp rating actually  gave you about 2 400  that you can get into your phone now i  do think that apples will be better than  45  efficiency with their better batteries  higher voltage and the magsafe  but doing some research most people say  that 70 is probably  the high end and quinn from snazzy labs  did some math as well and that is being  optimistic so if we do the math that  would mean that your iphone 12 will get  roughly  a 70 total charge from the power bank  and looking at these other options that  i reviewed  this one right here which is actually  the cheapest one gives you 68  percent so even with the extra  efficiency  you're not going to get a full charge  and on an iphone 12 pro max  that might be closer to about a 50  charge  only so that is definitely a bummer  but that wasn't the end of the world i  didn't buy it for  how much capacity it had i bought it  because i want fast wireless charging  most of these third-party options will  either give your iphone 7.5 watts  or 5 watts even though they'll say 15 or  20 that's only for android phones and  who would buy this for an android phone  and then that is the rated capacity  whereas i  tested what actually goes into your  phone after loss  and some of these will do seven on the  better end some will do six that are  less efficient  and then this one's rated five actually  gave you 3.5  where magsafe is more efficient it can  actually give you close to that  15 watts which is fantastic but this is  where  the story really turns for the worst if  we dig  into apple's support page it says that  yes you can get that really fast 15 watt  max save charging  but only if you're plugging a 20 watt or  higher cable  into it and using it as a wireless  charger  if you unplug it when you're on the go  you will only get  5 watts of rated wireless charging  so that comment that said they're  waiting for  uh apple's official one for fast  charging that's exactly what we were  waiting for  unfortunately that is just not the case  and even if apple can reach that five  watts of actual  wireless charging instead of 3.5 that is  still slower than the seven that you can  get  with this hyper power and we haven't  even talked about prices  just yet now what does that mean in the  real world  well in my actual ultimate comparison we  see  that 3.5 watts of real charging only  gets you 13  after 30 minutes and then the faster  7.5 that gives you seven into the phone  which is gonna be better than apples  only gives you 23 charge compared to  actual magsafe the way it should work  which will give you  30 charge in 30 minutes and even  more than that as far as how fast it  charges under  30 minutes and then after an hour max  safe would give you 55  but you will actually get somewhere  between  28 to 35 charge  in one hour so that is  really really slow so not only will you  get a low capacity from that battery  the charging speed will be much slower  but it actually gets  worse in one more way apple decided to  stick with lightning instead of going  with usb type-c  like with most of these third-party  options and that means that you cannot  get power out  any other way than wirelessly charging  which is much slower  much less efficient and you have less  capacity  with these options right here you can  plug a cable in if you have one and in  that case  you will get more capacity so this one  right here instead of charging 68  with an iphone 12 you will get 100  charge and it'll also be about three  times  faster to charge compared to wireless  charging so in those scenarios  you can use it as a standard fast  wireless charging  bank or just regular power bank unless  you need the convenience of not having a  cable  and with that you can plug in an apple  watch charger  any other you know lightning cable for  air pods an  android phone or anything else your  bluetooth speaker and you can get more  power whereas with apple's option  you can't do that it's only for wireless  charging the slow and less efficient  way and then comes in the price point  apple's cost a hundred bucks whereas  this guy right here i bought for  28 so this has similar capacity  and similar charging speed more  flexibility  and it is about you know a third of the  price less than a third of the price  and this one right here that has more  capacity this will charge 85 percent  it'll charge faster it comes in at 40  and it also has a usbc  output as well so let me know your  thoughts  of course we're going to get these in  i'm going to be putting to the test  hopefully they do better than what  they're advertised  but this info is from apple themselves  it's not from  anybody else so once we test it i'll do  my final review you guys click that  subscribe button above  if you guys 